# Robot safety

This harness talks to a **real** Flex (KansasFLEX). Follow `docs/safety-model.md`.

## Hard constraints

- Mutations default **off** (`ALLOW_MUTATIONS=false`). Require explicit enablement for installs, camera enable, etc.
- Enable access control only via `flex-test crs enable --confirm-one-way`
  (`PATCH /auth/settings/accessControlEnabled` is one-way; catalog probes never call it)
- CRS-on QA remote-access carveout (SSH/Jupyter while CRS stays on): documented in
  `docs/crs-testing.md`; CLI `flex-test serial allow-remote-access` requires
  `ALLOW_MUTATIONS=true`. Does not disable CRS; EXEC-2176 wipe is separate.
- Physical motion only via gated CLIs: `flex-test seed-runs` and
  `flex-test lpc-jog-timing --confirm-clear-deck` (both need `ALLOW_MUTATIONS=true`).
  Do not invent ungated home/move/jog commands or ad-hoc motion URLs.
- Live protocol **play** (homes / tip pickup) is allowed only when the user **explicitly** requests it, with deck preflight; prefer HTTP run actions and documented protocols under `docs/test-suggestions/protocols/`
- Use exclusive robot lock for scenarios that touch the robot
- All HTTP calls need timeouts via `RobotHttpSession` / settings
- Redact secrets in evidence; do not commit `.env` or credentials
- Prefer read-only clients/capabilities unless the user explicitly asks to mutate
- Re-verify `ROBOT_HOST` before mutating or playing (DHCP can change the IP)

## Risk levels

`READ_ONLY` → `REVERSIBLE_MUTATION` → `DISRUPTIVE` → `INSTALLATION` → `DESTRUCTIVE` → `PHYSICAL_MOTION`

Gate mutating work with `ensure_mutation_allowed`. Ungated home/move/jog
APIs stay rejected. Operator-requested motion uses `seed-runs` or
`lpc-jog-timing` (see `docs/safety-model.md`, `docs/known-state-and-latency.md`).
Live protocol play is documented in `docs/pyro-testing.md`.

## Robot identity

- Default display name: **KansasFLEX** (not "Kansas")
- Config: `ROBOT_HOST`, `ROBOT_NAME` in `.env` (gitignored)
